      "writtenOn": "2026-07-09T15:12:34Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "max_tso is the device\u0027s maximum TSO payload, but currently it is only checked for being nonzero. Could we store it and validate the payload in rdma_mlx5_try_tso() before posting the WQE? This remains outside the regular TX fast path. Allowing an oversized WQE to fail may put the QP into an error state, and the current completion path does not recover the queue. It would also be useful to log a warning at initialization when the device limit is below VPP\u0027s maximum GSO size.",
      "revId": "215bc930693a877bcbe53cb056f4e8e0e90f7070",
      "serverId": "6d2eb258-4fe2-443e-8a38-ca81da23d4c2"
    },
