      "writtenOn": "2026-07-09T15:12:34Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This is still difficult to reason about because rdma_mlx5_try_tso_or_regular() does not handle the regular case: REGULAR tells the caller to execute the large block below, while DONE can mean either posted or dropped.\n\nCould we extract the regular block into rdma_mlx5_tx_regular() and have one per-packet helper fully handle either path? The loop would then only need to distinguish CONSUMED from NO_SLOTS, keeping ownership, packet advancement, and tail accounting in one place.",
      "revId": "215bc930693a877bcbe53cb056f4e8e0e90f7070",
